Changes made: thirty seconds were cut from the original, starting at 1:10, and
re-encoded to 640x360 H.264 (CRF 26) with AAC stereo audio at 96 kb/s. Nothing else
was altered. The command, for anyone who wants to reproduce the file:

    ffmpeg -ss 70 -i BigBuckBunny_640x360.m4v -t 30 \
        -vf "scale=640:360,setsar=1" -r 24 \
        -c:v libx264 -preset slow -crf 26 -profile:v high -pix_fmt yuv420p -g 48 \
        -c:a aac -b:a 96k -ac 2 -ar 44100 \
        -movflags +faststart -map_metadata -1 \
        -fflags +bitexact -flags:v +bitexact -flags:a +bitexact \
        big-buck-bunny-30s.mp4

